31) Scaling risk estimates

The VaR(95) number calculated in previous exercises is simply the value at risk for a single day. To estimate the VaR for a longer time horizon, scale the value by the square root of time.

# Aggregate forecasted VaR
forecasted_values = np.empty([100, 2])
# Loop through each forecast period
for i in range(0, 100):
    # Save the time horizon i
    forecasted_values[i, 0] = i
    # Save the forecasted VaR 95
    forecasted_values[i, 1] = var_95*np.sqrt(i+1)
# Plot the results
